  "notes": "A formal word for holding or possessing something significant — weapons, assets, patents, or data. Not used for everyday personal belongings, where {持|も}つ or {所有|しょゆう}する are more natural.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {核|かく}{保有|ほゆう}{国|こく}: nuclear-armed nation\n- {株式|かぶしき}を{保有|ほゆう}する: to hold stocks\n- {保有|ほゆう}{数|すう}: number of holdings\n- データを{保有|ほゆう}する: to retain data\n- {保有|ほゆう}{者|しゃ}: holder, owner\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {所有|しょゆう}: ownership (legal ownership of property or goods)\n- {持|も}つ: to have, to hold (everyday, informal)\n- {所持|しょじ}: possession (carrying on one's person, often legal context)",
